      <Xref identifier="Q9S7H1" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="1135" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="brito, dreher, PMN, pmngroup">PSI-D interacts strongly with and plays an important function in the docking of ferredoxin. PSI-D binds tightly to PSI-C in plant PSI |CITS: [11687207]|. The Arabidopsis genome has two PsaD genes, |FRAME:AT4G02770| (AT4G02770) and |FRAME:AT1G03130| (AT1G03130) |CITS: [14996217]|.</Comment>
